# Paths excluded from scripts/prose_lint.py, one path prefix or exact path per
# line. Exclusions are for text this project does not author, for machine
# output, or for bytes something else binds. Never for authored prose that
# happens to be inconvenient to fix.

# Not this project's text.
.venv/
.git/
node_modules/
example-bundle/
to-delete/

# Fixtures and pinned upstream conformance data.
tests/

# Benchmark material whose CURRENT bytes a measurement receipt hashes, so that
# a published number stays tamper-evident. Editing any of it means re-running
# the benchmark, which changes what the numbers mean.
#
# Two groups in benchmarks/receipt.py, not one. `_OUTPUT_PATHS` lists the
# generated result documents. `_corpus_group` additionally hashes the measured
# corpus, `benchmarks/corpus/**/*.md` and `benchmarks/governance/**/*.md`, which
# is 290 files; they carry no findings today, and excluding them keeps a later
# well-meant prose fix from silently invalidating the receipt.
#
# The REST of benchmarks/ stays linted, including README.md and
# real_corpus_eval.md. Its Python sources are bound only through
# `SOURCE_PATTERNS`, which check_benchmark_docs.py verifies against the bytes
# committed at the receipt's own source_commit, read from git history, so
# editing a comment or a docstring today invalidates nothing.
benchmarks/corpus/
benchmarks/governance/
benchmarks/governance_results/ablation.md
benchmarks/governance_results/embeddings/ablation.md
benchmarks/results/report.md
